1	# Evento Framework — Complete Minimal Example (v2.1.0)
2	
3	A single-bundle order app under `com.study.app.*`, adapted from the `evento-lab`
4	reference. It demonstrates: one **aggregate** (two commands/events), one **projector** +
5	**projection** + **query**, one **saga** reacting to an event and sending a command, one
6	**observer**, and a **REST controller invoker** calling the gateways.
7	
8	This is the imitation template — every import is shown and the code compiles against
9	`evento-bundle:2.1.0` + Spring Boot 3.5.x. The `App` and `EventoConfiguration` classes are
10	the pre-wired skeleton (shown for completeness; do not modify them).
11	
12	Package layout (matches the mandated layers: `web`, `command`, `query`, `domain`, `config`):
13	```
14	com.study.app
15	├── App.java                         (@SpringBootApplication)
16	├── config/EventoConfiguration.java  (pre-wired bundle bean)
17	├── domain/command/  CreateOrderCommand, ConfirmOrderCommand     (payload types)
18	├── domain/event/    OrderCreatedEvent, OrderConfirmedEvent
19	├── domain/query/    FindOrderByIdQuery, ListOrdersQuery
20	├── domain/view/     OrderView
21	├── command/         OrderAggregate, OrderAggregateState, OrderService,
22	│                    OrderSaga, OrderSagaState, OrderObserver    (write/process side)
23	├── query/           OrderProjector, OrderProjection, OrderViewStore (read side)
24	└── web/             OrderInvoker, OrderController               (HTTP boundary)
25	```
26	
